.TH EZBIND 1 "2026-09-21" "ezbind 0.1.0-dev" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ezbind \- prepare an ebook PDF for folded-folio home bookbinding
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ezbind
.RB [ OPTIONS ]
.I INPUT.pdf
.B --output
.I OUTPUT.pdf
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ezbind
arranges an ebook PDF for duplex printing as folded single-sheet folios. The
sheets are folded with the fold toward the spine, stacked, and glued into a
text block. Physical cover cards, adhesive, and fabric are supplied and placed
by the user.
.PP
The canonical usage statement is:
.PP
.nf
Usage: ezbind [OPTIONS] INPUT.pdf --output OUTPUT.pdf
.fi
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --help , \-h
Print the usage statement, option summary, and exit-status summary. This
operation does not require an input PDF and returns status 0.
.TP
.BR --output \ OUTPUT.pdf
Write the imposed PDF to the specified path.
.TP
.B --force
Replace an existing output file. Without this option, an existing output is
not replaced.
.TP
.B --sheet letter
Use US Letter sheet dimensions.
.TP
.B --sheet a4
Use ISO A4 sheet dimensions.
.TP
.B --grid margin
Draw the default light-gray graph-paper-like vector grid in permitted margin
regions. The default spacing is 5 mm.
.TP
.B --covers blank
Add blank front and back cover-card pages. Cover pages are excluded by default.
.TP
.B --spine-guide line
Add an optional printed guide for the physical fabric/spine reserve.
.SH UNITS
Physical dimensions accept millimetres (mm), inches (in), and PDF points (pt).
Margins are measured from finished-page edges. The default margins are 12 mm
top and bottom, 15 mm at the fore-edge, and 20 mm at the spine.
.SH OUTPUT AND PHYSICAL WORKFLOW
The output contains two logical page positions on each side of each folded
sheet. The nominal four-page assignment is front-left 4, front-right 1,
back-left 2, and back-right 3. Pages are padded with blanks to a multiple of
four. Print duplex, fold each sheet once with the fold toward the spine, and
stack sheets in output order before gluing.
.PP
Printer duplex flip settings vary. Verify the page sequence and fold direction
with a small asymmetric test document before binding a valuable book.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error.
.TP
.B 3
Input PDF error.
.TP
.B 4
Impossible layout.
.TP
.B 5
Output or filesystem error.
.TP
.B 6
Missing or unusable runtime dependency.
.TP
.B 10
Unexpected internal error.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Usage errors are written to standard error and include the diagnostic followed
by the canonical usage line. Ordinary diagnostics do not include extracted
source text, passwords, or complete PDF content.
.SH PDF LIMITATIONS
Visible page content and selectable text are preserved through the qpdf backend
where supported. Annotations, interactive forms, bookmarks, tagged structure,
signatures, and other document-level features may be reported as degraded or
unsupported. Input PDFs that are malformed, empty, or unsupported are rejected.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
ezbind --sheet letter --grid margin book.pdf --output book-bound.pdf
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qpdf (1)
